    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50874" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">victŭālis</span></b> , e,
			adj.
		2. victus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to
			nourishment</i> or <i>sustenance</i> (postclass.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ministerium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Dogm. Plat. 1, p. 10, 17</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sumptus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cod. Just. 8, 51, 20</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">victŭālia</span></b> ,
			ĭum, n., <i>provisions</i>, <i>victuals</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Cassiod. Var. 3, 44</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4,
				5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg. 2 Macc. 3, 10</span></i>.</div>
